---
// Astro's i18n routing (`prefixDefaultLocale` + `redirectToDefaultLocale` in
// astro.config.mjs) emits its own `/` -> `/en/` redirect page at build time and
// refuses to build without a root index file to hang it on, so this file must
// exist. Its body is never shipped: the build warns that route `/` conflicts
// with a higher-priority route and drops it. It is kept as a plain meta-refresh
// fallback so switching the redirect option off still leaves `/` reaching `/en/`.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url=/en/" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="/en/" />
    <title>Redirecting...</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>Redirecting to <a href="/en/">English version</a>...</p>
  </body>
</html>
